title: The Opposition Platform
subtitle: You are in opposition. Fight the leadership openly, or keep your head down.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: rf_party
view-if: rf_platform_timer <= 0 and player_leads = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; rf_platform_timer = 3

= The Opposition Platform

The leadership is [+ leader_name +]. Your faction has [+ player_strength +]% of the party and dissent of [+ player_dissent +].

- @publish: Publish a platform and campaign for it in the locals.
- @appeal_moscow: Send the platform to Moscow instead of to the members.
- @accept: Accept the leadership's decisions for now.

@publish
on-arrival: {!
Q[Q.player + '_strength'] += 6;
Q[Q.player + '_dissent'] += 6;
Q[Q.leader + '_dissent'] += 4;
Q[Q.player + '_moscow'] -= 3;
!}

Your platform circulates in mimeographed copies. Members argue about it in every cell meeting. The leadership calls it factionalism, which it is.

@appeal_moscow
on-arrival: {!
Q[Q.player + '_moscow'] += 6;
Q[Q.player + '_strength'] += 2;
Q.autonomy -= 3;
!}

You send your criticism to the ECCI. It is a quieter road, and it teaches Moscow that the German factions will bring their quarrels to it.

@accept
on-arrival: {!
Q[Q.player + '_dissent'] -= 12;
Q[Q.player + '_moscow'] += 3;
Q[Q.player + '_strength'] -= 2;
!}

You announce that you will work loyally under the leadership. Some of your followers drift away. Moscow likes it.
